  "row-status": {
    "$description": "The Status dropdown's own value label, by the status of the row's record (Figma nodes 254:19537 Analysed, 254:19577 Submitted, 254:19618 Approved, 254:27048 Pending, 254:27129 Declined, 2026-09-22). A direct report (\"put back the default row background color to white as it was\") corrected the first pass at this (Figma 237:30119), which had tinted every cell in the row; every cell now stays var(--ds-color-bg-surface) regardless of status (table-cell/style.css) and only the pill inside the Status cell carries color (table-row/style.css). -text is the pill's label color (row-status primitives, Base-Primitives.json); -bg is that same color at Figma's own alpha over white (0.1, or 0.05 for declined, which Figma renders paler than the other four) -- not expressible as a token $value reference, so written as a literal rgba() here, same pattern as text.subactive above. No dark value exists yet: build.py emits these under :root:not([data-theme=\"dark\"]) and dark pills stay untinted.",
    "analysed-text": {
      "$value": "{row-status.analysed}",
      "$type": "color",
      "$description": ""
